    <bpmn:process id="W_W1561" name="W1561. BuildRight Brand Ambassador &amp; Pro Advocate Program, Trade Professional Community Building &amp; Referral Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual program design cycle; or top trade customer identified through loyalty analytics per W1452; or Store Manager nomination of exemplary trade professional
Frequency: Annual program enrollment; quarterly events and content production; monthly referral tracking
Volume: Target: 200–400 brand ambassadors across the Philippines (~1–2 per store); each ambassador reaches 50–200 peers through their professional network
Owner: VP Marketing
Participants: VP Marketing, Digital Marketing Manager, Trade Account Manager, Store Manager, Brand Ambassador (external trade professional)
Source: workflow W1561 — BuildRight Brand Ambassador &amp; Pro Advocate Program, Trade Professional Community Building &amp; Referral Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1561_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1561_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1561_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1561_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1561_Lane2" name="VP Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1561_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1561_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1561_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1561_Lane3" name="Digital Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1561_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1561_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1561_Start5" name="Annual program design cycle; or top trade customer identified through loyalty analytics…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1561_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1561_Task6" name="Ambassador recruitment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Ambassador recruitment: (a) selection criteria: (i) active trade account in good standing with &gt; PHP 500K annual purchases, (ii) strong local reputation (positive word-of-mouth in their professional community), (iii) willingness to publicly associate with BuildRight, (iv) social media presence (Facebook/Instagram account with project photos); (b) nomination sources: (i) Store Manager nominations (based on in-store relationship), (ii) Trade Account Manager recommendations, (iii) loyalty data per W1452 (top spenders by store); (c) VP Marketing approves each ambassador; (d) target: 1–2 ambassadors per store × 200 stores = 200–400 ambassadors
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Trade Account Manager / VP Marketing
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 20 hours (annual recruitment cycle)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1561_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1561_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1561_Task7" name="Ambassador onboarding &amp; benefits package">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Ambassador onboarding &amp; benefits package: Enrolled ambassadors receive: (a) &quot;BuildRight Pro Advocate&quot; identification card with exclusive benefits: (i) priority access to new products before general availability, (ii) annual invitation to BuildRight Pro Summit (networking event with key vendors and fellow advocates), (iii) Pro Advocate-exclusive discounts (additional 5% on top of trade pricing per W112 for select categories), (iv) direct hotline to Trade Account Manager for urgent orders or issues; (b) BuildRight Pro Advocate branded merchandise: branded hard hat sticker, vehicle decal, polo shirt; (c) Digital Marketing Manager creates ambassador profile page on buildright.com.ph (&quot;Meet our BuildRight Pro Advocates in [city]&quot;)
Responsible (R): VP Marketing / Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–3 hours/ambassador</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1561_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1561_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1561_Task8" name="Quarterly ambassador engagement events">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly ambassador engagement events: VP Marketing hosts quarterly events to maintain ambassador engagement: (a) regional networking dinners (4 regions: NCR, Luzon, Visayas, Mindanao) with Category Managers presenting upcoming product launches and promotions; (b) annual Pro Summit: 1-day event at Davao HQ or Manila venue with keynote by CEO/COO, vendor exhibitions, best-practice sharing among ambassadors, and recognition awards (Top Referrer, Most Engaged Advocate); (c) virtual events: monthly &quot;Pro Tips&quot; live session on Facebook where an ambassador shares a construction technique using BuildRight products — recorded and shared as content per W142
Responsible (R): VP Marketing / Digital Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 40 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1561_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1561_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1561_Task9" name="Referral tracking &amp; rewards">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Referral tracking &amp; rewards: (a) each ambassador receives a unique referral code; (b) when a new trade account is opened per W24 using an ambassador&#x27;s referral code: (i) new account receives welcome discount (5% off first purchase), (ii) ambassador receives referral reward: PHP 1,000 gift card or 500 bonus loyalty points; (c) monthly: Digital Marketing Manager tracks referral funnel: (i) referral codes issued → new accounts opened → first purchase → repeat purchase; (ii) top referrers recognized quarterly; (d) annual referral target: 500–1,000 new trade accounts through ambassador program (~10–20% of annual new trade account target)
Responsible (R): Digital Marketing Manager / Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1561_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1561_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1561_Task10" name="Annual program review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual program review: VP Marketing evaluates program ROI: (a) total referrals generated and conversion rate; (b) ambassador retention rate (target: &gt; 80% year-over-year); (c) program cost (benefits, events, rewards) vs. incremental revenue from referred accounts; (d) brand awareness impact: ambassador social media reach and engagement; (e) adjust benefits, events, and recruitment strategy for next year
Responsible (R): VP Marketing
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1561_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1561_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1561_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1561_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1561_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-283 (ensure controlled execution — Brand, PR &amp; Corporate Communications (PA-14.3).) | - operational: tying referral rewards to activity (no referrals = no renewal)
Owner: VP Marketing</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
