    <bpmn:process id="W_W1562" name="W1562. Crisis Communications &amp; Media Response Protocol for Product Recall, Safety Incident &amp; Public Relations Event" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Product safety recall notification from vendor or BuildRight quality testing per W150; or serious customer injury at store per W140; or media inquiry about a BuildRight-related incident; or viral social media post about a negative BuildRight experience
Frequency: Major crisis events: 1–3/year; minor incidents requiring media response: 5–10/year; product recalls: 2–5/year
Volume: Each event varies in scale; major crisis may involve multiple media outlets, government agencies, and legal proceedings
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Participants: VP Legal, CEO, VP Marketing, COO, Store Manager (if store-level incident), CHRO, External PR Agency, Legal Counsel, Customer Service Manager
Source: workflow W1562 — Crisis Communications &amp; Media Response Protocol for Product Recall, Safety Incident &amp; Public Relations Event</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1562_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1562_Lane1" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1562_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1562_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1562_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1562_Lane2" name="Crisis Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1562_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1562_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1562_Lane3" name="VP Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1562_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1562_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1562_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1562_Start5" name="Product safety recall notification from vendor or BuildRight quality testing per W150; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1562_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1562_Task6" name="Incident classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Incident classification: VP Legal classifies the incident severity: (a) Level 1 (Minor): isolated customer complaint with media inquiry potential; no injuries; limited scope (1 store); e.g., customer receives wrong pricing, stockout complaint goes viral on social media; (b) Level 2 (Moderate): customer injury requiring medical attention; product quality issue affecting multiple customers; negative media coverage initiated by local news; e.g., customer slips and breaks arm in store, batch of defective tiles reported by multiple customers; (c) Level 3 (Severe): serious injury or fatality; product recall affecting chain-wide inventory; government investigation; national media coverage; e.g., customer fatality from falling lumber, vendor issues product recall for electrical products with fire risk
Responsible (R): VP Legal
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1562_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1562_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1562_Task7" name="Crisis response team activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Crisis response team activation: Based on severity: (a) Level 1: VP Marketing + Store Manager manage; (b) Level 2: VP Legal + VP Marketing + COO + Store Manager + CHRO; (c) Level 3: Full crisis team activated — CEO + CFO + VP Legal + VP Marketing + COO + CHRO + External PR Agency + External Legal Counsel; (d) crisis team assembles within 1 hour (Level 2) or 30 minutes (Level 3) via emergency conference call; (e) VP Legal designates a single spokesperson (VP Marketing for media, VP Legal for legal/government matters) — all other team members must not speak to media or post on social media about the incident
Responsible (R): VP Legal
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1562_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1562_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1562_Task8" name="Initial fact gathering">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Initial fact gathering (within 2 hours of incident): Crisis team gathers facts: (a) what happened: detailed incident timeline (who, what, when, where, how); (b) who is affected: customer(s), employees, bystanders; (c) current status: injuries, medical treatment, store status (open/closed); (d) what are the legal and regulatory implications: DOLE reporting for workplace injuries per W140, BIR/DTI notification for product issues, LGU notification if required; (e) what is the media/social media situation: has the story been picked up? by whom? what is the social media sentiment?; (f) Store Manager provides firsthand account and all available documentation (CCTV footage, incident reports, transaction records)
Responsible (R): Crisis Team / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1562_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1562_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1562_Task9" name="Statement preparation &amp; approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Statement preparation &amp; approval: (a) VP Marketing prepares initial holding statement: (i) acknowledge the incident, (ii) express concern for those affected, (iii) state that BuildRight is investigating and will provide updates, (iv) provide media contact (VP Marketing or External PR Agency); (b) VP Legal reviews for legal accuracy and risk (admit no liability, preserve attorney-client privilege); (c) CEO approves statement for Level 2–3 incidents; (d) statement released within 4 hours of incident: (i) Level 1: social media response post, (ii) Level 2: press statement to local/national media + social media, (iii) Level 3: press conference or live statement by CEO + social media + website posting
Responsible (R): VP Marketing / VP Legal / CEO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1562_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1562_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1562_Task10" name="Ongoing crisis management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Ongoing crisis management (Day 2 onward): (a) daily crisis team briefing (Level 2–3) until resolved; (b) VP Marketing manages media inquiries: (i) all media inquiries routed to VP Marketing or External PR Agency, (ii) provide regular updates as investigation progresses, (iii) monitor social media sentiment and respond to misinformation; (c) COO manages operational response: (i) product recall execution per W150 if applicable (remove affected products from all 200 stores, notify customers who purchased the product), (ii) store remediation (repair safety issue, retrain staff), (iii) cooperate with government inspectors; (d) VP Legal manages legal response: (i) engage external legal counsel for liability assessment, (ii) prepare for potential litigation, (iii) manage insurance claim per W853; (e) CHRO manages employee communications and welfare
Responsible (R): Crisis Team
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Ongoing until resolved</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1562_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1562_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1562_Task11" name="Post-crisis brand recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-crisis brand recovery: After crisis is resolved: (a) VP Marketing develops brand recovery plan: (i) positive media outreach (what BuildRight did to fix the problem, safety improvements implemented), (ii) customer communication (affected customers receive personal outreach from Customer Service Manager per W41), (iii) community engagement (W1511 activities in affected community), (iv) social media content highlighting BuildRight&#x27;s commitment to customer safety; (b) VP Legal conducts post-crisis legal review: lessons learned, liability exposure assessment, insurance recovery status; (c) COO implements corrective actions: new safety procedures, vendor quality requirements, staff retraining; (d) CEO signs off on post-crisis report
Responsible (R): VP Marketing / VP Legal / COO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1562_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1562_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1562_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1562_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1562_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-283 (ensure controlled execution — Brand, PR &amp; Corporate Communications (PA-14.3).) | - operational: VP Legal &amp; Compliance review and approval gate
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1562_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1562_Annotation13" targetRef="W1562_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
