    <bpmn:process id="W_W5572" name="W5572. Undercover-Investigation &amp; Media-Exposé Response Protocol (Investigative-Newsroom Event)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Notice or credible discovery that a journalist, newsroom, or advocacy group is investigating BuildRight — an undercover applicant or contractor inside operations, hidden-camera footage offered or aired, a right-of-reply letter with a deadline, or an investigative series in pre-publication (labor practices, vendor sourcing, site safety, pest/sanitation footage, data handling)
Frequency: Rare: 0–2 active investigative threats chain-wide per year; right-of-reply letters are the common entry point and undercover placement the rare one
Volume: 1 event × the response team (comms, legal, the exposed function) × the reply-deadline window (48 hours – 7 days) × the remediation track where the exposed practice is real
Owner: VP Marketing / VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Participants: VP Corporate Communications, External PR agency (W1562 retainer), VP Legal &amp; Compliance, External Counsel, Data Protection Officer (VS-91 where footage captured personal data), HSE Manager / LP Director (site verification), CHRO (labor-practice claims), Internal Audit (VS-21 verification), Corporate Communications (W134/W143 execution)
Source: workflow W5572 — Undercover-Investigation &amp; Media-Exposé Response Protocol (Investigative-Newsroom Event)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5572_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5572_Lane1" name="VP Corporate Communications">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5572_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5572_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5572_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5572_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5572_Lane2" name="LP Director">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5572_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5572_Lane3" name="VP Legal &amp; Compliance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5572_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5572_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5572_Lane4" name="Exposed function&#x27;s VP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5572_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5572_Lane5" name="CHRO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5572_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5572_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5572_Start7" name="Notice or credible discovery that a journalist, newsroom, or advocacy group is…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5572_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5572_Task8" name="Intake &amp; log">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Intake &amp; log: the offer, letter, or footage reference is logged with source, outlet, deadline, and claims summary; a single response channel and spokesperson are named (W134 discipline); staff are instructed on the no-comment + forward-to-comms rule
Responsible (R): VP Corporate Communications
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: Day 0</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5572_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5572_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5572_Task9" name="Authentication sprint">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Authentication sprint: match claimed footage to site, date, and shift (uniforms, fixtures, PO/HR records); cross-check against CCTV (W838-class retrieval) and access logs; verify the undercover&#x27;s employment trail where one existed; the authentication record — confirming, refuting, or unresolved — is written before any public word
Responsible (R): LP Director / HR / Comms
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 24–72 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5572_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5572_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5572_Task10" name="Legal posture &amp; privilege">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Legal posture &amp; privilege: litigation hold on the relevant records; counsel-led response team; no document alteration or deletion (the cover-up is always the second story); assessment of personal-data duties where filming captured customers/employees (VS-91/W53)
Responsible (R): VP Legal &amp; Compliance / External Counsel
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Day 0–2</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5572_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5572_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5572_Task11" name="Right-of-reply assembly">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Right-of-reply assembly: facts-only written response to the specific claims — corrections with evidence, context without spin, remediation already under way stated with dates; the deadline is met or an extension negotiated in writing; draft passes through the VP Legal &amp; Compliance gate
Responsible (R): VP Corporate Communications / External Counsel
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Before deadline</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5572_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5572_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5572_Task12" name="Self-report calculus">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Self-report calculus: where authentication confirms a regulatory failing (safety, labor, waste, data), counsel weighs pre-emptive engagement with the regulator against waiting for broadcast; the default is early voluntary engagement with the remediation plan attached
Responsible (R): VP Legal &amp; Compliance / CHRO / HSE Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5572_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5572_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5572_Task13" name="Remediation activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Remediation activation: the exposed practice gets a named owner, a dated plan, and tracked milestones (audit-verifiable, not comms-verifiable); interim protections (e.g., immediate PPE, scheduling fix, vendor re-audit) execute before publication where possible
Responsible (R): Exposed function&#x27;s VP / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per plan</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5572_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5572_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5572_Task14" name="Source &amp; practice follow-through">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Source &amp; practice follow-through: no retaliation against any employee believed to be a source — suspected whistleblowers route to VS-119&#x27;s non-retaliation machinery; the undercover&#x27;s own misconduct (theft, trespass) is assessed for proportionate, documented action on counsel&#x27;s advice only
Responsible (R): CHRO / VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5572_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5572_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5572_Task15" name="Post-event review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-event review: coverage post-mortem (claims vs records, response timing, quote discipline); the authentication sprint&#x27;s gaps (CCTV coverage, access logs, contractor screening) feed corrective actions; a media-verification readiness note updates the W1562 crisis kit
Responsible (R): VP Corporate Communications / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2–4 weeks post</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5572_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5572_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5572_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5572_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5572_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-283 (ensure controlled execution — Brand, PR &amp; Corporate Communications (PA-14.3).) | - operational: every public response carries the VP Legal &amp; Compliance review gate; the authentication record is filed before any rebuttal; remediation milestones tracked to audit evidence, not comms claims
Owner: VP Marketing / VP Legal &amp; Compliance</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
